/-!
# Binary Mathieu code and cocode calculations: H.13–H.16

The source modules are the literal native Golay quotients. This assembly
currently exposes their constructions, the nondegenerate invariant pairing,
Golay self-duality, and the proved E.4.3 bounds `a ≤ 3`
for M₂₂/M₂₄ central quotients and the actual M₂₃ code/cocode restrictions.
The M₂₂ theorem retains the genuine central-cover and outer-extension
hypotheses of E.4.3.

The native local markings and the fixed-space-span dimension and transport
steps for H.16.8 are also provided. The native common four-group, its E16
coverage, and the compatible heptad/quintet Sylow marking are proved.
The native H.14.1–3 classification is assembled: the M24 E64 and large
elementary fusion statements, the sextet covering quotient and natural action,
the trio tensor and octad natural actions, the M23 semilinear and irreducible
actions, and the inner/outer M22 Sylow catalogues and natural/indecomposable
actions. The common field line has fifteen stabilizer conjugates. The native
involution classes and exact fixed sets from H.14.4 are also exposed.
The remaining code/cocode fixed-space calculations,
absolute irreducibility, and the code/cocode offender classifications are
remaining source obligations. In particular the conditional native-input
transport theorem is not an unconditional proof of H.16.8.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
H.13–H.16, printed pp.395–405 (the following printed page is blank).
-/
